Page: 1
Section: None
Text: We propose a simple way to use fuzzy and informal knowledge from experts to guide discovery of interpretable latent topics in text. The underlying intuition of our approach is that latent factors should be informative about both correlations in the data and a set of relevance variables speciﬁed by an expert. Mathematically, this approach is a combination of the information bottleneck and Total Correlation Explanation (CorEx).

